/**
@page commands Commands

@brief Shell command reference - the built-in commands typed at the `botanik>`
       prompt.

@note **Draft.** This page covers the current built-in command set only. It will
grow as site-specific commands are added; for now it tracks what
@ref Botanik::Shell::CommandShell ships with.

Commands are entered on the @ref Botanik::Pages::ShellPage "Shell" page. A submitted
line (see @ref md_docs_2KEYBINDINGS) is dispatched through
@ref Botanik::Shell::CommandShell::dispatch "dispatch()", falling through to the
built-in handler. An empty line is ignored; an unrecognized one echoes
`Unknown command: …`.

@section commands_builtin Built-in commands

| Command        | Action                                                                                                                       |
|----------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `help`         | Print the one-line list of available commands.                                                                               |
| `clear`        | @ref Botanik::Shell::ShellWriter::clear "clear()" - wipe the shell scrollback and redraw an empty prompt.                     |
| `stats`        | Dump scheduler/runtime counters (uptime, CPU load, jitter, stack usage/depth) from @ref Botanik::Scheduler::SchedulerContext. |
| `breakpoint`   | @ref Botanik::HAL::debug_break "HAL::debug_break()" - trap into an attached debugger.                                         |
| `reset`        | @ref Botanik::HAL::reset "HAL::reset()" - reboot the firmware (does not return; the simulator re-execs to the current page).  |

@section commands_extending Extending

Application code adds commands by subclassing @ref Botanik::Shell::CommandShell and
overriding @ref Botanik::Shell::CommandShell::dispatch "dispatch()": handle the
site-specific verbs there, then call the base so the built-ins still resolve. History
and kill-ring support are stubbed for now.
*/
